{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundled UI is intentionally opinionated. Each modifier picks the platform-appropriate presentation so consumers don’t have to repeat the conditional compilation themselves, and so the dispatch flow stays symmetric across platforms — the same "},{"code":".paywall(.dismiss)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" action fires from a "},{"code":"fullScreenCover","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on iOS and from a sheet on macOS."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This article explains the reasoning behind those choices and what is fixed versus configurable.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"revenueCatPaywall","anchor":"revenueCatPaywall","level":2},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Platform","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Presentation","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reason","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"iOS","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fullScreenCover"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A subscription paywall is a primary moment, not an interrupt. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fullScreenCover"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the UI immersive and prevents accidental gesture-dismiss."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"macOS"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sheet"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"frame(minWidth: 400, minHeight: 600)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mac sheets do not expand to fill the parent window. Without an explicit minimum size the paywall would render too small to legibly show plan options. The 400×600 minimum is roughly the size RevenueCatUI’s templates assume."}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because neither presentation offers a system dismissal affordance (","type":"text"},{"code":"fullScreenCover","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has no swipe-to-dismiss; Mac sheets have no default close control), the modifiers show ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s close button by default. Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"displayCloseButton: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only for a hard paywall the user must purchase through — and make sure some other path out of that screen exists.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The minimum frame is hard-coded; it is not exposed as a parameter. If your paywall layout needs more room on macOS, use "},{"code":"RevenueCatUI.PaywallView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly inside a custom ","type":"text"},{"code":"sheet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"revenueCatCustomerCenter","anchor":"revenueCatCustomerCenter","level":2},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Platform","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Presentation","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reason"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sheet"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatUI.CustomerCenterView"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"RevenueCatUI ships a customer center on iOS only. A non-fullscreen "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sheet"},{"type":"text","text":" is appropriate because customer-center actions are administrative, not part of a purchase flow."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"macOS","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Opens ","type":"text"},{"code":"itms-apps:\/\/apps.apple.com\/account\/subscriptions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then clears the request","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"RevenueCatUI does not ship a customer center on macOS, and the system has no equivalent in-app surface. The primitive modifier uses SwiftUI’s URL opener and fires ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDismiss"},{"text":"; the composed modifier dispatches the plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".openManageSubscriptions"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dismissCustomerCenter"},{"text":" actions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With the composed modifier, the macOS branch dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".openManageSubscriptions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", then clears the binding to dispatch "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dismissCustomerCenter"},{"type":"text","text":". The plugin’s URL opener is injectable, so apps and tests can control the external hand-off. The primitive binding-based modifier uses SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"openURL"},{"type":"text","text":" environment action and falls back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/apps.apple.com\/account\/subscriptions"},{"type":"text","text":" when nothing handles the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"itms-apps"},{"type":"text","text":" scheme."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Presentation coordination","anchor":"Presentation-coordination"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On iOS, the composed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"revenueCatPaywall(state:offeringIdentifier:displayCloseButton:purchaseLogic:send:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier never shows the paywall and customer center at once. The paywall wins: while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState.isPresented"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", the customer-center binding reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", and an initial or later state with both flags set dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dismissCustomerCenter"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On macOS, subscription management is an external App Store hand-off rather than a second modal surface. The customer-center binding remains active while the paywall sheet is open, so the composed modifier dispatches "},{"code":".openManageSubscriptions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and then "},{"code":".dismissCustomerCenter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" without losing the request."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apps wiring the primitive modifiers manually own the iOS exclusivity rule."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"One app-wide attachment","anchor":"One-app-wide-attachment"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach the composed modifier once, to one app-wide presentation host. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState"},{"type":"text","text":" is shared, so attaching the modifier inside every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WindowGroup"},{"text":" window or scene makes every copy respond to the same request. A multi-window app should choose one scene, such as its primary app or settings window, to own paywall presentation.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Why no platform-override hooks","anchor":"Why-no-platform-override-hooks","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both modifiers are deliberately parameter-light: an ","type":"text"},{"code":"isPresented: Binding<Bool>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", an optional "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDismiss: () -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":", and — on the paywall only — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"displayCloseButton:"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"offeringIdentifier:"},{"text":", and optional app-owned ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"purchaseLogic:"},{"text":". There is no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"paywallStyle:"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"presentationKind:"},{"text":" parameter.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The reasoning: any consumer that needs to deviate from the chosen presentation already has the underlying RevenueCatUI types (","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"CustomerCenterView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and SwiftUI’s full presentation surface (","type":"text"},{"code":"sheet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"fullScreenCover","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"popover","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", custom containers). The bundled modifiers exist to handle the 95% case in one line — when the 5% case applies, drop down to RevenueCatUI directly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This package does not try to be the complete paywall-UI library. It is the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"integration layer"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" that makes the common case trivial."}]},{"text":"What is configurable","anchor":"What-is-configurable","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The configurable surface lives in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatUI"},{"text":" and on the paywall plugin:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Paywall content, copy, and template","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — configured in the RevenueCat dashboard. ","type":"text"},{"code":"RevenueCatUI.PaywallView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" renders whichever offering and template the dashboard returns."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Customer-center labels, sections, and actions","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — configured in the RevenueCat dashboard. ","type":"text"},{"code":"RevenueCatUI.CustomerCenterView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" renders whichever configuration the dashboard returns.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Close button"}]},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"displayCloseButton:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the paywall modifiers. Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":"; pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" for a hard paywall."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Presentation triggering"}]},{"text":" — driven by the plugin via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState.isPresented"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isCustomerCenterPresented"},{"text":". Your code chooses ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"when","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" to set them via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".request(reason:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".presentCustomerCenter"},{"text":" actions.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dismiss behavior"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — dismiss actions are dispatched by the presentation bindings themselves (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dismiss"},{"text":" for the paywall, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dismissCustomerCenter"},{"text":" for the customer center). The primitive modifiers’ ","type":"text"},{"code":"onDismiss","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" callbacks are purely additive — use them for analytics hooks or cleanup, not for dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Offering selection"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"offeringIdentifier:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the paywall modifiers presents a specific RevenueCat offering (a win-back or regional offer, for example). Omit it for the dashboard’s current offering. An unknown identifier or a failed fetch falls back to the current offering with a logged warning, so a stale identifier degrades gracefully instead of dead-ending the purchase flow."}]}]}]}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"revenueCatPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"revenueCatCustomerCenter"},{"type":"text","text":" modifiers present differently on iOS and macOS, and what is hard-coded."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI"},{"type":"text","text":" documentation provides the matching API reference for the modifiers described here."}],"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToPresentTheUI"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping"],"anchor":"Explanation"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/PlatformBehavior"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/platformbehavior"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Platform Behavior","role":"article"},"references":{"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"RevenueCat adapter for Swidux’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Implements ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against ","type":"text"},{"code":"Purchases.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", ships a controllable mock for previews and tests, and pairs with "},{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for drop-in "},{"code":"PaywallView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"CustomerCenterView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" presentation."}],"title":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall"},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/EntitlementMapping":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How RevenueCat’s "},{"code":"CustomerInfo.entitlements","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" translates to Swidux’s "},{"code":"EntitlementSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Entitlement Mapping","kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/entitlementmapping"},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/HowToPresentTheUI":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/howtopresenttheui","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"revenueCatPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"revenueCatCustomerCenter"},{"text":" view modifiers from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI"},{"text":" to a root view, driven by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"How to Present the UI","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToPresentTheUI"}}}